+### ASO-specific functions
+
+In addition to the standard CEL functions and libraries above, ASO provides the following function under the `aso`
+namespace. The `aso` namespace is used to avoid collisions with any user-defined identifiers.
+
+#### `aso.parseResourceId`
+
+`aso.parseResourceId(string)` parses an ARM resource ID string and returns a `ResourceID` object. If the string is not a
+valid ARM resource ID, the expression fails with an error.
+
+The returned `ResourceID` object exposes the following fields:
+
+| Field               | Type           | Description                                                                 |
+|---------------------|----------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
+| `subscriptionId`    | `string`       | The subscription ID.                                                        |
+| `resourceGroupName` | `string`       | The resource group name.                                                    |
+| `provider`          | `string`       | The resource provider.                                                      |
+| `location`          | `string`       | The resource location, if present.                                          |
+| `name`              | `string`       | The resource name.                                                          |
+| `resourceType`      | `ResourceType` | The resource type, with nested `namespace` and `type` string fields.        |
+| `parent`            | `ResourceID`   | The parent resource ID for hierarchical IDs (recursive), if present.        |
+
+For example, to extract the subscription ID from a resource's ARM ID:
+
+```
+aso.parseResourceId(self.status.id).subscriptionId
+```
+
+Or to extract the resource type namespace:
+
+```
+aso.parseResourceId(self.status.id).resourceType.namespace
+```
+
 
